      "syllabusTopic": "Soybean (Glycine max): origin, distribution, economic importance, varieties, and Bradyrhizobium inoculation",
      "questionText": "Provide an extensive package of practices for commercial soybean production, covering seedbed preparation, varietal selection, inoculation, weed control, and post-harvest handling.",
      "modelAnswer": "Soybean (*Glycine max* (L.) Merr.) is the dominant rainfed kharif oilseed in Central India. Achieving yields exceeding 2.5 t/ha requires meticulous execution of agronomic practices.\n\n### 1. Soil and Seedbed Preparation\nSoybean thrives in well-drained, fertile black clay soils (Vertisols) and loamy soils with pH 6.5\u20137.5. It is extremely sensitive to waterlogging. The seedbed must be prepared by one deep summer plowing followed by 2\u20133 harrowings to produce a fine, firm tilth. Sowing on the Broad Bed and Furrow (BBF) system (beds of 1.2\u20131.5 m width separated by 30 cm furrows) or Ridge-and-Furrow configuration is strongly recommended to facilitate drainage during intense monsoon downpours and conserve moisture during dry spells.\n\n### 2. Varietal Selection\nSelect varieties adapted to local agro-climatic zones:\n- **Early Maturing (85\u201395 days):** JS 93-05, JS 95-60 (suited for low-rainfall or late-onset monsoon tracts).\n- **Medium Duration (95\u2013105 days):** JS 335 (wide adaptation, shatter-tolerant), NRC 37 (Ahilya 2), NRC 127 (shatter-resistant, high oil).\n- **Disease-Resistant Cultivars:** DSb 21 (resistant to rust and pod blight).\n\n### 3. Sowing and Inoculation Protocol\n- **Seed Rate & Spacing:** 65\u201375 kg/ha for medium-sized seed lots (100-seed weight 10\u201312 g); row spacing of 45 cm and plant-to-plant distance of 5\u20137 cm (target population: ~400,000 plants/ha); sowing depth should not exceed 3\u20134 cm.\n- **Seed Treatment (FIR):** Treat first with Thiram + Carbendazim (2:1 @ 3 g/kg), followed by Imidacloprid 600 FS (3 ml/kg). Lastly, inoculate with *Bradyrhizobium japonicum* culture and Phosphate Solubilizing Bacteria (PSB) @ 10 g/kg seed using a 10% jaggery sticker solution.\n\n### 4. Nutrient and Weed Management\n- **Fertilization:** Recommended dose is 25:60:40:30 kg N:P2O5:K2O:S per ha applied basally. Sulfur application via gypsum (200 kg/ha) is critical for oil and methionine synthesis.\n- **Weed Control:** Critical period of weed competition is 15\u201335 DAS. Pre-emergence spray of Pendimethalin 38.7% CS @ 1.0 kg a.i./ha or post-emergence application of Imazethapyr 10% SL @ 100 g a.i./ha at 15\u201320 DAS controls annual grasses and broadleaf weeds.\n\n### 5. Harvesting and Post-Harvest Seed Care\nHarvest when leaves turn yellow and drop, and pods turn golden brown (seed moisture 14\u201315%). To protect delicate embryos from micro-cracking, set thresher cylinder speeds strictly below 350\u2013400 rpm. Dry seeds gently to 9\u201310% moisture before storing in clean, moisture-proof gunny bags.",
